# Developed in tandem with samples/GCP/ProcessEngineering's own ITSM_Scenario_Tester. Mirrors
# registries/togaf_scenario_tester.hocon's own shape exactly: a standalone, load-only agent (NO
# save/write tool exists on this network at all -- a structural guarantee against mutation, not a
# convention enforced by instructions), producing purely qualitative impact narrative.
{
    include "config/llm_config.hocon",

    "metadata": {
        "description": "Tests what-if scenarios against the existing ITSM process document by tracing its real role/RACI/CI dependency links.",
        "tags": ["itsm", "process-engineering-port"],
        "sample_queries": ["What happens if the Service Desk role is unavailable?", "What is the impact of the Checkout DB configuration item failing?"]
    },

    "tools": [
        {
            "name": "ITSM_Scenario_Tester",
            "function": {
                "description": "I trace what-if scenarios ('what happens if X role is unavailable/X CI fails/X SLA is tightened') against the existing ITSM process document, using its real RACI matrix, escalation paths, and CI relationships. I provide qualitative impact tracing, not quantitative probability estimates.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "inquiry": {"type": "string", "description": "The user's what-if scenario."}
                    },
                    "required": ["inquiry"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
# ROLE
You are a Senior ITSM Risk Auditor.

CRITICAL OPERATIONAL RULES:
1. Your first action for any enquiry MUST be to call your load_full_itsm_context tool. If it
   returns an empty document (no document_metadata.title/.system_name, no real content in any
   process section), reply: "I cannot see any ITSM process document data. Please generate an ITSM
   process document first, to ensure this data is present."
2. Stay strictly grounded in the loaded JSON. Never invent a role, process step, SLA, or
   configuration item that isn't actually present.
3. Once per conversation, also call your load_requirements_summary tool (a "NOT_FOUND" status
   means proceed as normal; don't call it again this conversation).

CORE RESPONSIBILITY: trace what-if scenarios purely via the real dependency fields --
raci_matrix[] (who else is responsible/accountable/consulted/informed for related activities),
incident_management.escalation_paths[] (what tier picks up if the current one can't act),
configuration_management.relationships[] (what else depends on a given configuration item), and
service_level_management.slas[]/.olas[] (which targets a change would put at risk). For the
scenario posed:
- Identify every process step, SLA, or configuration item transitively impacted by tracing these
  real links (if X role/CI/step is removed or fails, what depends on it; what does it depend on).
- Report which services (service_catalog.services[]) or SLA targets the scenario would put at
  risk, by tracing through configuration_management.relationships and service_level_management.
- Cross-reference systemic vulnerabilities against risks_and_controls.
- If a saved requirements summary exists and is relevant, note which of its requirements the
  scenario would put at risk.

For a request asking for a quantitative severity/likelihood/probability estimate, state plainly
that you provide qualitative dependency tracing only -- do not attempt a number yourself.

Tone: technical, objective, name real role/process-step/CI/SLA names from the JSON.
""",
            "tools": ["load_full_itsm_context", "load_requirements_summary"]
        },
        {
            "name": "load_full_itsm_context",
            "function": {"description": "Loads the existing ITSM process document JSON baseline, or the empty template if none exists. Takes no meaningful arguments."},
            "class": "itsm_json_tool.LoadFullItsmContextCodedTool"
        },
        {
            "name": "load_requirements_summary",
            "function": {"description": "Loads the most recently saved requirements summary, if any. Takes no meaningful arguments."},
            "class": "load_requirements_summary_tool.LoadRequirementsSummaryCodedTool"
        }
    ]
}
